From 311f4d4ed9efa4cba7e0e1a8948c8814543c510a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:23:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the reasons and the advice of the player information
 fit their labels

The labels of the player information neither wrap nor scroll (a label that scrolls would
draw the whole GUI again on every frame while the page is open), so a text wider than its
label is cut. Measured with the skin's own font at the size of each label:

- the sentence at the top (1628 px, font12) cut "Not sent as Dolby Vision: the converter
  of the board is not on the list of those seen working with Dolby Vision (set ...)",
  whose second half repeats the advice of the line under it, in every language;
- the advice under it (font10) cut the Spanish of "To try it, set Dolby Vision through a
  display converter to On ...", by a few pixels;
- the row "Why not native" (540 px on the overview, 530 on the Dolby Vision page, font10)
  cut four of its reasons in English and five in Spanish: the converter turned off, the
  converter not on the list, the SDR base layer that could not be composed, the HLG base
  layer whose RPU declares no PQ picture, the driver that lacks something (530 px), and in
  Spanish "its own HDR10+ was chosen".

They say the same in fewer words ("this board's converter is not known to work"; "the SDR
base layer could not be composed": the standard is in the log), in en_gb and in es_es,
es_ar and es_mx, whose msgid is the new English.

Host test (outside the tree): measure.py builds every text these labels can show (the
variables of the skin expanded) in the four languages and measures it with
NotoSans-Regular at the size of the label: before, 7 texts are wider than the heading
labels and 39 than the reason rows; after, none. msgidsync.py: the Spanish files
translate the English of en_gb.
